  <h1>Approaches to Belief</h1>
  <blockquote style="font-size:1.14rem">"Come now, and let us reason together, saith the Lord."<cite>{% scripture "Isaiah 1:18" %}</cite></blockquote>
  <p class="ab-lede">This is not an argument. It is a map.</p>
  <p>Somewhere on it is the place you actually stand — not the place someone assumed you stand, and not the place you would be assigned by the label you happen to carry.</p>
  <p>Whatever you believe when you arrive here, you are welcome. Theist, atheist, agnostic, or genuinely unsure — every one of those positions is argued in this resource by its own best reasons, sourced to the thinkers who actually made them. Including the objections mine has to answer.</p>
  <p>Seven sections. Roughly forty minutes at a steady pace, or as long as you like. There is a reflection at the end of each one; nothing is graded, nothing is sent anywhere, and nothing is stored beyond your own browser.</p>
  <div class="ab-notes"><h4>Facilitator</h4><ul>
    <li>Set the frame before advancing: <em>nobody here is being converted; we are locating ourselves honestly.</em></li>
    <li>If the group is mixed, say so out loud. It earns the room.</li>
    <li>Arrow keys or Space advance. Press <b>P</b> to toggle Present mode.</li>
  </ul></div>
