    <div class="ab-fb" data-fb="s5">
      <b>Merognostic.</b> Two claims held at once: something real <em>is</em> known, and the knowing is admittedly partial. The agnostic would not say "I have felt God answer me." The gnostic would go on to describe heaven. This is the distinction most often collapsed — partial knowing gets mistaken for no knowing, and people conclude they have lost their faith when they have only grown honest about its edges.
    </div>
