<article class="ab-slide" data-sec="sum" data-label="Two paths">
  <img loading="lazy" class="ab-ico" src="/assets/studies/approaches-to-belief/icons/atb-13.jpg" alt="A dirt footpath dividing into two through tall grass.">
  <div class="ab-eyebrow"><span class="ab-num">Where to go from here</span></div>
  <h2>Two honest next steps</h2>
  <p>Everything to this point has been reasoning. What follows is not — and you may take either path, or neither, and remain entirely welcome.</p>
  <div class="ab-fork">
    <div class="ab-forkcard" data-fork="experiment">
      <b>1 · Run the experiment</b>
      Test the claim rather than accept it. Set a commitment, a start date, and a date to evaluate honestly. Roughly thirty days.
    </div>
    <div class="ab-forkcard" data-fork="long">
      <b>2 · Read the long version</b>
      Everything compressed here is developed at length in the first six chapters of <em>Words of Plainness</em> — the search for meaning, academic knowledge, spiritual knowledge, sincere prayer, and faith in Jesus Christ.
    </div>
  </div>
  <div id="ab-forkExperiment" style="display:none">
    <h3>The experiment</h3>
    <p>Just as the natural faculties allow beliefs to be tested by observation and application, spiritual knowledge allows for a kind of sacred experiment that produces observable outcomes. Three scripture verses summarize this, escalating in what they ask and what they promise:</p>
    <div class="ab-verse"><b>"If any man will do his will, he shall know of the doctrine, whether it be of God."</b><small>{% scripture "John 7:17" %} — a conditional claim with a predicted result. Not <em>feel better</em>. Know.</small></div>
    <div class="ab-verse"><b>"He that hath my commandments, and keepeth them… I will love him, and will manifest myself to him."</b><small>{% scripture "John 14:21" %} — the deeper promise</small></div>
    <div class="ab-verse"><b>"Even if ye can no more than desire to believe, let this desire work in you."</b><small>{% scripture "Alma 32:27" %} — the honest entry point. You do not need conviction to begin.</small></div>
    <div class="ab-act ab-personal">
      <span class="ab-tag">Set it down</span>
      <h3>Approach A: Put it into practice and see for yourself.</h3>
      <p style="font-size:.97rem">Thirty days is a good length. There are two honest ways to run it — either one is a real experiment:</p>
      <div class="ab-card"><b>1 &middot; Practice something new</b><span>Pick one to three commandments of Christ and keep them deliberately for the period you set.</span></div>
      <div class="ab-card"><b>2 &middot; Examine something you already do</b><span>Pick one to three behaviors you already practice, and observe honestly how they affect you and the people around you — measured on the ecological scale of good and evil from Section 6.</span></div>
      <p class="ab-q">What will you do? Name the commandment or behavior specifically. If you need help choosing, open the <a href="https://commandments.brotheraaron.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Keep My Commandments &#8599;</a> web app and browse until you find a few that are to your liking.</p>
      <input type="text" data-j="goal-what" placeholder="e.g. Daily prayer, morning and evening, in my own words">
      <p class="ab-q">Start date</p>
      <input type="date" data-j="goal-start">
      <p class="ab-q">Date you will stop and evaluate honestly</p>
      <input type="date" data-j="goal-review">
      <p class="ab-q">Decide now, before you begin: what would you accept as a result? What would you <em>not</em> be entitled to conclude either way?</p>
      <textarea data-j="goal-criteria" placeholder="I would count it as a result if…"></textarea>
    </div>
    <div class="ab-act ab-personal">
      <span class="ab-tag">Set it down</span>
      <h3>Approach B: Seek personal revelation from God.</h3>
      <p>The second path to direct personal discovery of spiritual truth is discussed in greater depth in my writings, <a href="/chapters/04-spiritual-knowledge/#two-paths-to-confirmation">Chapter 4: Spiritual Knowledge</a>.</p>
      <blockquote>"You can learn to reach outside of yourself with your mind and heart, praying with sincerity to perceive truth spiritually. Ask if God is really there. There is no need for memorized phrases or complicated communication. Just speak what is in your mind and heart. He will listen."</blockquote>
      <p class="ab-q">How would you prepare yourself for such a prayer, and what would you ask?</p>
      <textarea data-j="goal-prayer" placeholder="How I would prepare, and what I would ask…"></textarea>
    </div>
    <small><b style="color:var(--inkGoldD)">About Keep My Commandments</b> — a daily discipleship tracker. Choose a commandment, mark the days, and keep your own record of what happens. If you would rather see what it is before opening it, <a href="/discipleship/#commandments">read about it here</a>.</small>
  </div>
  <div id="ab-forkLong" style="display:none">
